.TH WREX-IPV4 7 "2026-10-18" "wrex 0.1.0" "wrex Manual"
.SH NAME
wrex-ipv4 \- ipv4 layer for \fBwrex\fR(1)

.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwrex\fR \fIcraft\fR|\fIsend\fR [options] \fB--layer\fR \fIipv4\fR \fB--ipv4\-<field>\fR=\fIVALUE\fR ...
\fBwrex\fR \fIfields\fR \fIipv4\fR

.SH DESCRIPTION
IPv4 (RFC 791). Also a valid stack start. ver=4, ihl derived from options length (explicit ihl wins; invalid values are kept and flagged only under \-\-strict), total_len and checksum autofilled from the packet (explicit values win). proto drives the chain: 1=icmp, 6=tcp, 17=udp, else synthesized `unknown`. Stacks on eth or vlan (802.1Q tag). options grammar: eol,nop,rr:IP,ssrr:IP,lsrr:IP,ts:FLAG,CNT, or hex:BYTES. CLI alias: `ip` (\-\-ip\-ttl == \-\-ipv4\-ttl).
.

.SH ENCAPSULATION
Rank 20; stacks on eth, vlan (parents).

.SH "FIELD FLAGS"
Dots in field paths become dashes in flags (ipv4.ttl -> --ipv4-ttl, --ipv4-ver).
Explicit values always win over autofill and are kept
unvalidated; \fB\-\-strict\fR re-validates (violations exit 2).
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-ver=\fIINT\fR\fR
version (autofill: 4) Type u8. Default: 4.
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-ihl=\fIINT\fR\fR
header length in 32\-bit words (autofill: derived) Type u8. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-tos=\fIINT\fR\fR
type of service Type u8. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-total_len=\fIINT\fR\fR
total length (autofill: computed) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-id=\fIINT\fR\fR
identification (autofill: 0, deterministic) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-flags\fR
flags aggregate [df,mf]; per\-bit subpaths flags.df / flags.mf Type flagset. Default: 0.
Bit names (MSB first): df, mf. Aggregate \fB\-\-ipv4\-flags\fR sets the whole unit; per-bit \-\-ipv4\-flags\-df sets one bit.
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-frag_off=\fIINT\fR\fR
fragment offset Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-ttl=\fIINT\fR\fR
time to live (autofill: 64) Type u8. Default: 64.
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-proto=\fIINT\fR\fR
protocol (autofill: derived from next layer) Type u8. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-checksum=\fIINT\fR\fR
header checksum (autofill: computed) Type u16. Default: 0.
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-src=\fIIP\fR\fR
source address (autofill: 127.0.0.1; interface primary on send) Type ipv4. Default: 127.0.0.1.
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-dst=\fIIP\fR\fR
destination address (autofill: 127.0.0.1) Type ipv4. Default: 127.0.0.1.
.TP
\fB\-\-ipv4\-options\fR
options: eol,nop,rr:IP…,ssrr:IP…,lsrr:IP…,ts:FLAG,CNT, or hex:… Type bytes. Default: .

.SH EXAMPLES
wrex craft \-\-format hex \-\-layer eth \-\-layer ipv4 \\\\
  \-\-ipv4\-src=127.0.0.1 \-\-ipv4\-dst=127.0.0.1 \-\-ipv4\-ttl=63
# CLI alias: \-\-ip\-ttl=63 == \-\-ipv4\-ttl=63

.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBwrex\fR(1), \fBwrex\-eth\fR(7), \fBwrex\-arp\fR(7), \fBwrex\-vlan\fR(7), \fBwrex\-icmp\fR(7), \fBwrex\-udp\fR(7), \fBwrex\-tcp\fR(7), \fBwrex\-dns\fR(7)
